This product is designed to work with, and draws on ideas from, the following
open-source projects. No source code from them is included in this release yet;
when code is adapted, the file will carry the original copyright header and
this list will say which files.

- Ollama (https://github.com/ollama/ollama), MIT License: local model runtime (used as a separate program).
- Agent S (https://github.com/simular-ai/Agent-S), Apache-2.0: planned GUI-agent engine for GPU machines.
- UI-TARS Desktop (https://github.com/bytedance/UI-TARS-desktop), Apache-2.0: design reference (archived Nov 2026).
- Bytebot (https://github.com/bytebot-ai/bytebot), Apache-2.0: design reference for the task API (archived Mar 2026).

Models are downloaded separately by the user and carry their own licenses
(e.g. Qwen3 and Qwen2.5-VL: check each model page on ollama.com before redistributing in an ISO).

The Odeifried install image (ISO) is a Debian 13 derivative. It contains unmodified Debian packages
(each under its own license, see /usr/share/doc/*/copyright in the installed system), built with
live-build, installed with Calamares, and using the Xfce desktop, the Orchis GTK theme, Papirus icons
and the Inter font. It also includes hardware firmware from Debian's "non-free-firmware" section:
free of charge and redistributable, but not open source. Debian is a trademark of Software in the
Public Interest; Odeifried is not affiliated with or endorsed by Debian.

System tools used at runtime: xdotool, scrot, ImageMagick, zenity, AT-SPI (each under its own license).
